// a struct slot takes nothing but that struct. the parser used to reject this while *typing* the
// literal, with the same bogus "Unexpected token 'integer_literal' found" that made a literal
// unwritable in a generic body (todo/B11) - a type it cannot type a literal against is now simply
// not a hint, so the diagnostic belongs to the semantic pass, which is also the only place that
// can answer it for the generic below: `T $x = 42;` is fine for T=int32 and wrong for T=Point

struct Point
{
    int32 $x;
    int32 $y;
}

function make<T>() : T
{
    T $x = 42;
    return $x;
}

Point $p = 42;

Point $q = make<Point>();
